  <static seed="1923" source="Contrib/PCC/BasicMath/IntegerAndSquareRoot/identifySquareNumbers10.pg">
    <statement><p>Which of the following are square numbers?  There may be more than
one correct answer.</p>
<p><var form="checkboxes">
<li>
<p><m>136</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>46</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>25</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>49</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>120</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>144</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><p>You can quickly find the first few square numbers on scratch paper:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   1^{2} \amp = 1 \\
   2^{2} \amp = 4 \\
   3^{2} \amp = 9 \\
   4^{2} \amp = 16 \\
   5^{2} \amp = 25 \\
   6^{2} \amp = 36 \\
   7^{2} \amp = 49 \\
   8^{2} \amp = 64 \\
   9^{2} \amp = 81 \\
   10^{2} \amp = 100 \\
   11^{2} \amp = 121 \\
   12^{2} \amp = 144 \\
\end{aligned}
   }</m></p>
<p>It would be very helpful if you can memorize the above 12 square numbers.</p>
<p>So the correct answers are CDF.</p>
</solution>
